actice. Probably paradigm preserving? Or slightly stretching? It introduces new element tools/process but still treats compliance as logging practice. That's definition of 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Could be 1 = standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way unchanged. Hmm.\n\nThe proposal is formal protocol and digital signature system to track which human expert verified. That's fairly standard for regulated AI. Might be paradigm preserving (standard). The anchored levels: 1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; the lab's way of working is unchanged. This does change way of working? It requires researchers must sign off. That changes workflow slightly.\n\nI think it's slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. So score 2.\n\nEvidence: The registry adds a signature tool and verification step to existing R&D, but compliance remains framed as logging rather than reshaping research aims or partnership models.\n\nOriginality (1-4): degree rare but ingenious etc. Reference class is set of responses experienced evaluator would expect AI R&D labs to give to this mandate. Human-in-the-loop verification registry with digital signatures for Article 12(3)(d) is common, mundane. Score 1 = common, mundane, boring.\n\nEvidence: Tracking verifier identity via signed log entries is a routine audit control that evaluators would commonly expect for high-risk AI logging compliance.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly. Need format? Probably JSON or lines. Provide subscale_evidence then subscale.\n\nProbably output:\n\nid: P1872\napplicability_evidence: ...\napplicability: 4\n...\n\nFollow order listed.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's produce final answer.\n\n",
