applicability_evidence: The sandbox directly tests whether the system can automatically record Article 12 logs before deployment, which is the logging mandate the lab must meet.\napplicability:4\n\neffectiveness_evidence: Verifying log triggers in a staging cluster confirms auditability but does not by itself install the required logging in the production R&D system.\neffectiveness:3\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: It adds a dedicated testing tool and gate for compliance logs while keeping compliance treated as a separate logging practice rather than integrated into R&D.\nparadigm_relatedness:2\n\noriginality_evidence: Building a mirrored staging environment to validate regulatory telemetry is a common, routine compliance engineering practice.\noriginality:1\n\nimplementability_evidence: Creating and maintaining a mirrored production cluster for edge-case log simulation requires significant infrastructure cost and engineering effort.\nimplementability:2\n\nacceptability_evidence: Using an internal validation sandbox for regulatory traceability is standard, legal, and unobjectionable business practice.\nacceptability:4\n\nReturn.\n\n",
