        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\n\nWe need rate proposal P1284.\n\nProposal: Compliance-as-Code CI/CD Integration. Automated pipeline extracts training parameters, hyperparameters, validation results directly into required technical documentation format. Links version control to regulatory reports. Integrate MLflow or W&B with custom export script triggers upon every model registry update. Auto-populate general characteristics and limitations sections. Ensures technical documentation is kept up-to-date without adding manual overhead.\n\nWe need six subscales.\n\nparadigm_relatedness: degree to which idea preserves/modifies paradigm.\nAnchors:\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged\n\nProposal is automated pipeline linking version control to regulatory reports, auto-populate documentation. This introduces tools but still treats compliance as logging practice? It changes relationship somewhat? Compliance-as-Code integrates compliance into CI/CD. That is maybe slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice. Not changing relationship fundamentally? Might be paradigm stretching because logging woven into science? Hmm.\n\nIt links version control to regulatory reports. That's more than standard logging practice? Might be 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging prac