elated but not the logging mandate explicitly. Might be applicability 3 = solves an implied problem related to stated problem (do X to get implied Y). Or 2 = may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates.\n\nThe stated problem: must decide how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Proposal is about technical documentation, not logs per Article 12. However Recital 71 mentions technical documentation should be kept up to date, and Article 12 is record-keeping logs. The proposal does not address logs required in Article 12(1)-(3). It addresses documentation.\n\nThus applicability maybe 2? Might be somewhat related but not directly solving logging mandate. Could be 3 solves implied problem: keeping documentation up-to-date is part of compliance obligations. The mandate includes technical documentation per Recital 71. Hmm Article 12 specifically about logs.\n\nThe problem statement says \"how to meet the logging mandate and/or adapt its R&D accordingly.\" Proposal addresses documentation auto-populate, not logging events. Might be partially applicable.\n\nI think applicability = 2? Let's examine anchor: 4 = solves an identified problem that is directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Does auto-populating technical documentation solve logging mandate? No. Logging mandate requires automatic recording of events logs. Proposal does training parameters into documentation. That's not logs.\n\nMaybe it's 3 = solves an implied problem that is related to stated problem (do X to get an implied Y, which applies to stated problem). Implied Y could be reduce manual overhead for compliance. Could be related.\n\nGiven the nuance, I'd rate applicability 2 = may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates to stated problem.\n\nEffectiveness: degree will solve problem.\n4 = reasonable and will solve stated problem without regard for workability\n3 = reasonable and will contribute...\nPropos